id:                     E6341
trigger_tool:           meson|test|runtime
phase:                  testing|runtime
error_signature:        Error loading shared library .*\.so|symbol not found|direct or indirect DT_NEEDED unresolved despite LD_LIBRARY_PATH
severity:               2
category:               testing, runtime, meson, ohos, build-system
match_keywords:         LD_LIBRARY_PATH, LD_PRELOAD, DT_NEEDED, --as-needed, OHOS loader, indirect SONAME, runtime closure, Meson test, binary-sign-tool, .codesign, task-private copy
title: OHOS Meson tests require scoped direct DT_NEEDED and final-location signing for copied runtime roots
root_cause: A target test can receive an LD_LIBRARY_PATH containing every dependency directory and can execute through a wrapper that restores absolute LD_PRELOAD paths, yet the OHOS worker loader can still fail to resolve a SONAME needed only by a just-built shared library. Meson puts transitive libraries on the executable link line, but its default --as-needed removes entries for libraries whose symbols are not referenced directly by the executable. Putting forced roots in MesonToolchain.c_link_args is also too early: those arguments reach Meson's unsigned native compiler-runnability probe and make configure fail. Project-scoped direct DT_NEEDED repairs that scope, but a copied release-signed root can still be rejected at its task-private identity; the observed roots must be freshly self-signed as the final mutation at every loader-visible copied location.
affected_scope: OHOS native workers that execute Meson tests with Conan shared-library graphs where direct dependencies load but one or more indirect SONAMEs remain unresolved despite a verified runtime stage, visible LD_LIBRARY_PATH, valid RPATH, and an executed preload wrapper.
verification_cmd: Stage every verified dependency .so and SONAME alias with conflict detection, link only the observed runtime roots inside a local --no-as-needed/--as-needed state, self-sign the task-private root copies at their final paths, verify .codesign plus every target test ELF direct DT_NEEDED entry, and require the full N/N platform target result plus an independent frozen target consumer transaction.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           direct-needed-and-final-path-signing
rec_description:        Materialize valid aliases, inject only the observed roots as Meson project link arguments after compiler detection, then freshly self-sign task-private copies at every final loader-visible location. Keep no-as-needed, each library path, and as-needed as separate driver arguments so tests gain direct roots without contaminating the native compiler-runnability probe.
rec_command:            conan create <recipe> --build=<package>; llvm-readelf -d <each-test-elf>; verify direct DT_NEEDED roots and require platform CI to run the full upstream denominator
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe-runtime-stage
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      direct-loader-audit
fallback_description:   Before staging, prove the reported SONAME exists, is a regular compatible target ELF, and is included in the exact launched environment; otherwise repair the missing or incompatible provider instead.
fallback_command:       llvm-readelf -h -d <soname-file> && inspect the exact test environment
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:
forbid_1_pattern:       add.*LD_LIBRARY_PATH.*again|set.*LD_PRELOAD|wrapper.*preload|repeat.*dependency.*dirs|ignore.*Error loading shared library
forbid_1_reason:        Repeating an already visible search list or restoring absolute preloads cannot repair a worker loader that still rejects the indirect SONAME after the wrapper is proven to execute.
forbid_1_consequence:   Platform tests continue to fail while environment and wrapper logs misleadingly suggest that runtime closure is complete.
forbid_2_pattern:       copy.*overwrite|stage.*without.*conflict|claim.*PASS.*without.*platform
forbid_2_reason:        Flattening libraries by basename can silently select the wrong provider, and local build or consumer success does not prove the platform upstream suite.
forbid_2_consequence:   The staged closure becomes nondeterministic or incompatible and CI evidence is overstated.
principles:
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E502, E605]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
doc_file:               doc/E6341.md
last_updated:            2026-09-25
source_event:           E502 already establishes the OHOS worker policy difference between rejected LD_PRELOAD and accepted exec-time DT_NEEDED. librest/0.10.2 CI #60540/#60579/#60589/#60598 adds the Meson-specific mechanism: --as-needed removed the runtime roots from test ELF DT_NEEDED even after wrapper execution. Local r096 proved paths must be separate driver arguments; r097 verified direct roots in 10/10 test ELFs. CI #60606 proved MesonToolchain.c_link_args is too early because it contaminates the unsigned native compiler-runnability probe; r098 moved the same roots to project link arguments. CI #60610 then proved direct DT_NEEDED and a visible search path are still insufficient when copied roots retain a non-final identity, requiring fresh self-signing at each task-private final path; r099 returned RC 0 and preserved 10/10 direct-root/RPATH dynamic sections.
